# Response headers for Cloudflare Pages. Pages reads this file at build time and
# does not serve it. Paths are matched in order; `/*` is every response.
#
# The page loads nothing from anywhere - no fonts, no scripts, no analytics - so
# the policy below can deny every fetch and then name the two exceptions the
# page actually uses: its own inline <style>, and the favicon, which is a data:
# URI in the markup. If a future edit adds an external asset, the browser will
# refuse to load it until this file says otherwise. That is the point.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'; img-src data:; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
